{"name":"Candyland","title":"Candyland","revision":227109,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Candyland","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Candyland is a setting, often found in children's media, where the world, including buildings, the natural environment, and sometimes even people, are made of sweets. For example, the clouds are made of cotton candy, the buildings from gingerbread, etc."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This land is used to express whimsy. Artists use their imaginations to imagine how miniature, colorful candies can construct a large environment that replaces common images such as trees."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Note that this is called \"Level Ate\" on TVTropes, where you can find examples."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wreck-It Ralph (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cinnamoroll The Movie (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Barbie: Dreamtopia (2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candy Land: The Great Lollipop Adventure (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory (1971)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Amazing Digital Circus (\"Candy Carrier Chaos!\")"},{"kind":"list","text":"Adventure Time"},{"kind":"list","text":"One Piece (Whole Cake Island)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cookie Run franchise"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candyland"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candy Crush"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candy Makeup Party Salon"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mario Kart 8 and Mario Kart 8 Deluxe (Sweet Sweet Canyon)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mario Kart 8 Deluxe (Sweet Sweet Kingdom)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brawl Stars (Candy Land)"},{"kind":"list","text":"We Love Katamari (Gingerbread House)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kirby's Dream Buffet (2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rayman (Candy Château)"}],"contentS